[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"ocr\",\n    \"term\": \"OCR (Optical Character Recognition)\",\n    \"title\": \"What is OCR? Optical Character Recognition Definition | ToolTari\",\n    \"description\": \"Learn the definition of Optical Character Recognition (OCR), how text extraction works under the hood, and how to convert scans to text.\",\n    \"category\": \"ai\",\n    \"definition\": \"Optical Character Recognition (OCR) is a technology that converts different types of documents, such as scanned paper documents, PDF files, or images captured by a digital camera, into editable and searchable text data.\",\n    \"explanation\": \"OCR engines process pixel arrays to identify the characters, letters, and numbers printed in a document. The software scans the visual patterns of dark and light areas on a page to segment the image into text elements. Modern OCR systems utilize deep neural networks (like Convolutional Neural Networks and LSTM recurrent layers) to recognize characters in context, which significantly increases recognition accuracy on low-contrast prints or complex document layouts.\",\n    \"technical_details\": [\n      \"Image Binarization: The converter transforms color or grayscale pixels into binary black-and-white layouts to separate characters from background noise.\",\n      \"Deskewing: The algorithm rotates tilted text blocks to align lines horizontally, helping word boundary analysis.\",\n      \"Character Segmentation: Detects spacing to separate text paragraphs into distinct lines, words, and individual character shapes.\",\n      \"Neural Classifiers: Feeds pixel grids into network nodes to classify the shape as specific letters, validating outcomes against digital dictionaries.\"\n    ],\n    \"examples\": [\n      \"Converting a JPEG photograph of a paper invoice into a clean plain text (.txt) file containing lines of numbers and item details.\",\n      \"Scanning a legacy textbook using a digital scanner and using OCR to compile it into a searchable EPUB or PDF document.\"\n    ],\n    \"relat